 ## Background
-The concept of training neural radiance fields was introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2020 [S3, S4, unofficial]. Subsequent works like Mip-NeRF [S1] and DONeRF [S1] refined these configurations to address specific issues such as aliasing and training stability. NeUDF [S1] adapted these configurations for distance field representation.
+The original NeRF hyperparameters were established in the seminal NeRF paper [S3, S4, unofficial]. Mip-NeRF details were introduced in the Mip-NeRF paper [S1]. DONeRF was proposed to address computational efficiency in neural radiance fields [S2]. NeUDF and NeRF-SDP configurations are derived from their respective publications [S1, S2].
 
